From 0257059c8f38e6b3ea2620cecac45390b4af6a63 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cameron Basham <cambash23@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:12:51 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 109/110] glm cuda: the DFlash2 drafter MLP split across every
 rank (FF / world), the partials summed in rank order

dflash_load split the drafter's MLP only at world == 2 (gate and up by rows, down by K, ff = FF / 2) and dflash_block
summed the two fp32 halves with df_sum2; at world 4 every rank ran the whole 12,288-wide MLP of all five layers on every
block pass, 5.5 ms a round at one stream and 8.7 at four (TF_GLM_PROF, four GB10s on a switch), the one piece of the
round the ranks did not share.

dflash.mlpSplit(world) decides: any world that divides FF into 256-aligned shares splits (2: 6144 as before, 3: 4096,
4: 3072, 6, 8, 12, 16; the q4 pack's rows, glm_mm's K tiles and df_swiglu's columns all fit), one rank or a world that
does not runs the MLP whole. The loader slices rank r's gate and up rows and down columns at r * ff; rawBytes and the
weight estimate follow ff; the gathered partials buffer is [world][MAX_M][D] fp32; df_swiglu's grid is cdiv(ff, 1024).
df_sumn(g, out, R, world) replaces df_sum2: out = g[0] + g[1] + ... + g[world - 1] in rank order, one fp32 add a rank,
then one bf16 rounding, so at world 2 it is df_sum2's single add on the same two operands (same bits) and at any world
every rank holds the same sum. The extra gather (M x D x 4 bytes a rank: 128 KiB at one stream, 1 MiB at eight) goes
through the group, so it rides the RoCE path of the patch before this one when that is on, NCCL otherwise.

Exactness: drafts only propose tokens; the target verifies them, so the verified tokens cannot change (hashes
fab1d3b6894b / e71492bf766b must repeat). What can move is the drafter's own arithmetic: a rank's down partial sums its
3,072-wide slice in glm_mm's order instead of 12,288 in one, and the four partials add in rank order, so the drafted
candidates may differ in the last bit of a logit and the acceptance rate may move by a fraction of a percent; measured
with the recipe's acc.py "accepted" column (53% prose / 72% code today at four).

Tests: glm_dflash_host pins mlpSplit at every world 1-16 (halves at two, quarters at four, 4096 at three, whole at 5 and
7, every rank's slice inside FF, the shares the whole width, 256-aligned) and the raw scratch's sizing follows it; the
launch record for df_sumn carries df_sum2's register figures (refresh them with tf-cuda-test contract-limits on the first
image). To be measured on the Sparks: the drafter block's ms a round (TF_GLM_PROF / TF_GLM_DFLASH2_PROF) at one and four
streams against 5.5 / 8.7, acc.py's accepted column, and the two hashes.
